{"tutor":{"setspec":[{"name":["JWP B5SF_p98"],"lessonname":["B5SF p98"],"userselect":["false"],"stimulusfile":["JWP_stims_params_subset98.json"],"lfparameter":["0.85"],"shuffleclusters":["0-29"]}],"unit":[{"unitname":["Consent form"],"unitinstructions":["<font size=\"2\">Consent to Use Data<br><br>The Mechanical Turk task you have selected is part of a research project that is described below.  You will use your computer for this experiment, first to load the program, then to practice 48 Japanese-English word pairs repeatedly, then you will complete the posttest after a 2 day delay, at which time you will see 48 concluding word pair presentations. This study should take approximately 25 minutes total to complete. <br><br>\r\nIf you should have any questions about this research study please feel free to contact  Philip Pavlik at 901-678-2326. For questions regarding the research subjects' rights, the Chair of the Institutional Review Board for the Protection of Human Subjects should be contacted at 901-678-2533.<br><br>\r\nAll efforts, within the limits allowed by law, will be made to keep the personal information (your Amazon Turk Worker ID) in your research record private but total privacy cannot be promised. We will deidentify your data (remove your ID) after the experiment before storing it on our computers long-term. By participating, you understand and agree that the deidentified data gathered during this study may be used by University of Memphis and published and/or disclosed by University of Memphis to others outside of University of Memphis. However, no personally identifying information will ever be mentioned in any such publication or dissemination of the research data and/or results to other researchers.<br><br>\r\nBy clicking this button, I consent to the above terms.\r\n"]},{"unitinstructions":["Memory for Japanese vocabulary<br><br>\r\n            <b>Please read all of the text below carefully, it necessary to successfully complete the task.</b><br><br>\r\n             Task: You learn 30 different Japanese-English word pairs by repeatedly studying them for 20 minutes.<br>\r\n -For each pair, you will initially study the complete pair.<br>\r\n -On subsequent trials for a word pair, you will be asked to fill in the missing English word '__________'.<br>\r\n -On fill-in-the-blank trials, you must hit ENTER key after typing to submit your response.<br>\r\n -Try to guess or remember the answers for the blanks, and if you cannot guess, just press ENTER to read the correct answer.<br>\r\n -If you get a fill-in-the-blank answer wrong, you will be given a review with the correct answer for 4 seconds.<br>\r\n -You have 7 seconds when reading for study and 7 seconds to begin typing the answers for fill-in-the-blank trials.<br>\r\n -Please make sure this window is maximized before you begin.<br>\r\n When you are ready, press continue button to proceed to the next screen.   "],"unitname":["Model Unit"],"learningsession":[{"clusterlist":["0-29"],"unitMode":["thresholdCeiling"],"calculateProbability":["\r\n               // Base5s/Base5f params: c(0.2365, 0.0145, 0.0861, 0.1137, 0.1301, 0.1720, .0145, .0861, .1137, 1)\r\n                // A demonstration of a variable that will be shown in the console\r\n                p.CUSTOM_MSG = \"In our custom function\";\r\n\r\n                //Base5suc (d is positive here because it is denominator\r\n                p.baseLevelS = 1 / Math.pow(1 + p.questionSecsPracticingOthers + ((p.questionSecsSinceFirstShown - p.questionSecsPracticingOthers) * 0.0145),  0.2365);//par1 and par2\r\n                p.meanSpacingS = 0;\r\n                if (p.questionStudyTrialCount + p.questionTotalTests == 1) {\r\n                    p.meanSpacingS = .1137*10; //Use par4 in here?\r\n                } else {\r\n                    if (p.questionStudyTrialCount + p.questionTotalTests > 1) {\r\n                        p.meanSpacingS = Math.max(\r\n                                1, Math.pow((p.questionSecsSinceFirstShown - p.questionSecsSinceLastShown) / (p.questionStudyTrialCount + p.questionTotalTests - 1), 0.0861)//par3\r\n                                );\r\n                    }}\r\n                p.intbsS = p.meanSpacingS * p.baseLevelS;\r\n\r\n               // Base5fail (d is positive here because it is denominator\r\n                p.baseLevelF = 1 / Math.pow(1 + p.questionSecsPracticingOthers + ((p.questionSecsSinceFirstShown - p.questionSecsPracticingOthers) * 0.0145),  .1720);//par1 and par2\r\n                p.meanSpacingF = 0;\r\n                if (p.questionStudyTrialCount + p.questionTotalTests == 1) {\r\n                    p.meanSpacingF = .1137*10; //Use par4 in here?\r\n                } else {\r\n                    if (p.questionStudyTrialCount + p.questionTotalTests > 1) {\r\n                        p.meanSpacingF = Math.max(\r\n                                1, Math.pow((p.questionSecsSinceFirstShown - p.questionSecsSinceLastShown) / (p.questionStudyTrialCount + p.questionTotalTests - 1), 0.0861)//par3\r\n                                );\r\n                    }}\r\n                p.intbsF = p.meanSpacingF * p.baseLevelF;\r\n\r\n                // Helpful to be able to see our y parameter for debugging\r\n                \r\n                //logit\r\n                //p.logit = Math.log(1+p.questionSuccessCount)/Math.log(1+p.questionFailureCount)\r\n                \r\n                \r\n                //p.overallOutcomeHistory.length\r\n                //IEStemplate.xml has example\r\n                //\r\n//console.log(\"success counts\")\r\n//console.log(p.questionSuccessCount)\r\n//console.log(\"failure counts\")\r\n//par5 in log()\r\n                p.y = p.stimParameters[0] + 6.261 * p.intbsS * Math.log((0.1301*10)+p.questionSuccessCount) + 3.955 * p.intbsF*Math.log((1*10)+p.questionFailureCount+p.questionStudyTrialCount); //avg subj int //+ .908*p.logit\r\n       \r\n//console.log(\"p.y without parseFloat\")\r\n \r\n// At a minimum we need to set p.probability and return p\r\n                \r\n                p.probability = 1.0 / (1.0 + Math.exp(-p.y));  // Actual probability\r\n     \r\n                return p;\r\n            "]}],"deliveryparams":[{"practiceseconds":["300"],"drill":["7000"],"purestudy":["7000"],"skipstudy":["false"],"reviewstudy":["4000"],"correctprompt":["500"],"fontsize":["2"],"studyFirst":["true"],"correctscore":["1"],"incorrectscore":["0"],"timeuntilaudio":["500"]}]},{"unitname":["Show the questions"],"unitinstructions":["Demographic Survey<br><br>\r\nThank you for completeing the previous task. To finish up, please answer the following quick demographic questions, which may be useful for us to understand the data we collect."],"buttonorder":["fixed"],"deliveryparams":[{"drill":["12000000"],"purestudy":["4000"],"skipstudy":["false"],"reviewstudy":["4000"],"correctprompt":["500"],"fontsize":["3"],"correctscore":["0"],"incorrectscore":["0"],"ignoreClusterMapping":["false"],"timeuntilaudio":["500"]}],"buttontrial":["false"],"assessmentsession":[{"conditiontemplatesbygroup":[{"groupnames":["A"],"clustersrepeated":["1"],"templatesrepeated":["9"],"group":["\r\n                0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0\r\n                0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0 0,b,t,0"]}],"initialpositions":["\r\n             A_1 A_2 A_3 A_4 A_5\r\n             A_6 A_7 A_8 A_9"],"randomizegroups":["false"],"clusterlist":["30-38"],"assignrandomclusters":["false"],"permutefinalresult":["0-0"]}]},{"turkemailsubject":["Link for 2$ Bonus for Turk HIT"],"turkemail":["\r\nDear Amazon Turk Worker,\r\nRecently you completed part 1 of a 2 part experiment called 'Memory for Japanese', which paid $3.25. Now we would appreciate it if you would please return do part 2. It is less work than part 1, but we pay a $2.00 bonus for completion, since it is so important for us to get the part 2 data. This must be completed in the next 48 hours from when you get this email.\r\nPlease avoid typos in yo